[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: No program outside the daemon reads corpus content from disk

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-DAEMON-IS-THE-ONLY-SOURCE
TITLE: No program outside the daemon reads corpus content from disk
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
No program outside the scribe daemon reads corpus content from disk. Corpus
content is the .sdoc nodes, the grammar, the UID-to-path map, and the
semantics model. A consumer obtains all of it from the daemon over RPC, or it
does without.

A check that validates the corpus in the Nix sandbox is not a consumer of it:
the sandbox has no daemon, and the checks are what prove the bytes the daemon
serves.

This is not satisfiable today. The semantics layer is not defined well enough
to encode, so the representation the daemon would serve does not yet exist.
Until it does, the board's model.json read stands as a recorded violation
rather than a sanctioned exception.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One parsed, validated graph is the thing every consumer should reason from,
and the daemon already holds it. Every second reader of the same bytes is a
second parser with its own view: the board and the CLI each re-parse
grammar.sgra with an 81-line regex reader that cannot see strictdoc's injected
TEXT element, and the board walks the whole worktree for .sdoc files on every
generation change to rebuild a UID-to-path map the daemon could hand it. Two
views of one file drift, and the drift is invisible until a surface shows
something the other does not.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Operator, 2026-09-09, verbatim: "ideally i want everything going through the
daemon ... even board shouldn't read the disk directly for the sdoc contents
including semantics, ever. id call that a requirement, just not satisfiable
right now because we dont have the semantic layer defined well enough to
encode. i dont want you just filling in that until ive made it definable
through nix." And on the path map: "the daemon should be injecting the path,
board shouldn't be walking that."

Violations at the time of writing, measured 2026-09-09: the board parses
grammar.sgra (docs/sdoc/board/source.py:88), walks the worktree for .sdoc
files via uid_paths (source.py:91, through adapter.py:75 importing
docs/sdoc/view/view-check.py by path), and reads model.json through
semantics_payload (source.py:116); the CLI parses grammar.sgra for its
argparse surface (dev/scripts/scribe_cmd.py:335) and reads model.json for
`scribe semantics` (scribe_cmd.py:228); the view tooling parses grammar.sgra
(docs/sdoc/view/wireline.py:349, view-check.py:934).

Once the semantics representation exists and the daemon serves it, the second
paragraph of the STATEMENT is deleted and the model.json reads become plain
violations to fix. Extends DEC-SCRIBE-DAEMON-NO-FALLBACK and
DEC-SDOC-BOARD-READS-THE-SCRIBE-DAEMON, which forbid a second GRAPH and a
fallback LOAD but say nothing about reading corpus bytes directly;
MECH-SCRIBE-COMMANDS-LOAD-IN-PROCESS previously justified the client-side grammar read as "needs no corpus"; this requirement withdraws that carve-out. The daemon bootstrap remains unimplemented on this branch.
<<<
